WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.830
- Okay first of all, you're a genius.

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.670
Like this whole thing is ingenious.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.380
How did you come up with just,

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.590
getting people on your show.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.880
Watching celebrities
just be like (yelling).

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.713
- Like burn their mouth.

00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:10.560
How do they agree to that?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.393
I love it.

00:00:11.393 --> 00:00:13.740
- Well, the real genius
is my partner in all this,

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.420
Chris Schonberger, and
he runs First We Feast,

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:18.177
and he came up to me and was like,

00:00:18.177 --> 00:00:19.460
"You know I have this idea,

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.150
what if we were interviewing celebrities,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.830
but eating increasingly spicy,

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.664
like violently hot chicken wings."

00:00:24.664 --> 00:00:25.920
(laughing)

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.160
While the interview is going on,

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.900
and the way it hit my ear was just like,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.500
so funny to me that I'm like, all right,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.480
let's get in a room and
bang this whole thing out,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.858
shoot a pilot and go.

00:00:33.858 --> 00:00:35.031
- That's amazing!

00:00:35.031 --> 00:00:37.340
Who are like some of
your most memorable ones?

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.110
- Well there are a lot.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.490
We've done almost 200
episodes at this point,

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:42.323
believe it or not.

00:00:42.323 --> 00:00:44.980
But if I were to try and
get somebody into the show,

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.900
it's like if you watch
the Paul Rudd episode,

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.420
or like the Gordon Ramsay,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.255
or Charlize Theron, Scarlett Johansson.

00:00:51.255 --> 00:00:52.378
- [Rita] It's crazy!

00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:53.970
- If you like those episodes,

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.160
you'll probably like the show.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.410
So those are the ones I recommend.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:59.130
- Wait so has anyone just ever just like,

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.420
passed out, vomited, run to the bathroom,

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.304
like any of these things.

00:01:02.304 --> 00:01:03.137
- Yeah, check, check.

00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:04.230
Yeah we have like a whole,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.104
royal flush, like a whole
tic-tac-toe game that we can play.

00:01:07.104 --> 00:01:07.937
- Oh my God!

00:01:07.937 --> 00:01:08.770
It's like who is gonna make it?

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:09.603
Or what is gonna happen with them.

00:01:09.603 --> 00:01:10.436
- Yeah , I always think,

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:13.240
like our first studio was in
kind of this office building,

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.950
and around the studio,
it'd just be people like,

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.280
on computers, answering
phones, returning e-mails.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.930
And then like, very famous people,

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.158
would just come like
barreling out of the door.

00:01:24.158 --> 00:01:24.991
(laughing)

00:01:24.991 --> 00:01:25.824
Like, "Where's the restroom?

00:01:25.824 --> 00:01:26.657
Where's the restroom?"

00:01:26.657 --> 00:01:28.090
And I always thought it would be funny,

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.840
that they must be, "what
did they do in that room?"

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.854
- Oh my God!

00:01:31.854 --> 00:01:33.930
They are like "nobody come in here!"

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:34.770
Oh my gosh.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:36.370
Do you know anybody that's done this show?

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:39.340
- I know, I mean I know Charlize,

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.670
I haven't seen her episode though.

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:42.030
I'm gonna have to check that one out.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:42.863
- Classic episode.

00:01:42.863 --> 00:01:43.710
- Very, I mean like,

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:45.109
you have a couple of Oscar
winners in there, yeah.

00:01:45.109 --> 00:01:46.749
- Yeah.

00:01:46.749 --> 00:01:48.010
(applause)

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:50.620
- So why do you think,
do you think celebs go

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.860
because they feel challenged?

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.320
Like they are gonna conquer it?

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:54.153
- Well I think it is.

00:01:54.153 --> 00:01:55.731
- I mean that might be
what I'm thinking today.

00:01:55.731 --> 00:01:56.564
(Laughing)

00:01:56.564 --> 00:01:59.090
- You probably are in that same mindset,

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.740
where it's like, I think if you watch it,

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:02.580
there is part of you that wonders,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.818
could I handle that?

00:02:03.818 --> 00:02:04.651
- Yes!

00:02:04.651 --> 00:02:06.170
- Or how would I handle that spice.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.649
So I think, there are people that,

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:09.320
they're curious about it.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.490
But I think the thing is that,

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.260
we really try to extend for our guest,

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.100
meet 'em half way with a very thoughtful,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.390
career spanning interview like.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.223
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:16.223 --> 00:02:18.299
- We want it to be the
most, the most comfortable.

00:02:18.299 --> 00:02:19.132
(laughing)

00:02:19.132 --> 00:02:21.590
Uncomfortable interview is
what we really try to do.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.423
So I think there's a part of you.

00:02:22.423 --> 00:02:23.256
- You're throwing them off.

00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:24.089
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:24.089 --> 00:02:24.990
- It's hard to keep a
wall up when you're like,

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.280
hah ha ha ha.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.120
- Yeah, and I think there
is something about it,

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.490
that interrupts the formality of it all.

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:31.660
Like if you're doing anything,

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.330
even if you're trying to like,
balance books in your hand,

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.610
like maybe there is something about that,

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.280
that takes your mind off
of the sort of interview,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.720
into a realer place.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.710
- Yes, so you're turning
hot ones a game show,

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.115
which is brilliant.

00:02:43.115 --> 00:02:44.470
- Thank you.
(applause)

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.891
- Like it's the most brilliant move.

00:02:45.891 --> 00:02:48.480
And that one lady on that clip,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.310
legit, ate a wing like a giraffe eats.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:53.530
Like she put it in and
came out just a bone,

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:54.430
I was so impressed.
- [Sean] Right.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.240
- And she's skinny, I'm like all right.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.880
I wouldn't have thought
that was gonna happen.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.230
But I mean is that, what
is the game show like?

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.580
- Well I think that if I were
to try to connect the two,

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.130
because they are very different shows,

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.680
- One's like a classic
interview show over spicy wings,

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.510
the other classic game
show over spicy wings.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:10.200
But the way that I think about it is,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.550
the appeal of the interview show,

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.960
is it takes celebrity,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.390
this thing that's
inherently, by definition,

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:17.950
some sort of like
unobtainable, lifestyle status.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:20.040
And then it takes that person down,

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.060
to a level that everyone understands.

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.680
Which is dying on hot sauce.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.800
- Yes
- That's so true.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.540
- And then the game show,

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.810
takes that person, the person watching,

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.210
and exalts them into a hero status,

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.260
because they can conquer the wings,

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.380
and then make it to the top of
this game show, win $25,000.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.248
So that's where I think,

00:03:37.248 --> 00:03:38.081
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:03:38.081 --> 00:03:38.914
- That's where I think, they connect.

00:03:38.914 --> 00:03:41.323
But otherwise, like
totally different shows,

00:03:41.323 --> 00:03:42.156
different vibes.

00:03:42.156 --> 00:03:42.989
- Have you ever done the thing, where,

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.781
"and you folks at home can play along too!

00:03:45.781 --> 00:03:48.400
Here are the hot peppers or spices,

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.613
that we're gonna be using today!".

00:03:49.613 --> 00:03:51.217
- I think you just got a
good tip for your show!

00:03:51.217 --> 00:03:52.050
- No that was,

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:52.911
if you can help us thread that needle.

00:03:52.911 --> 00:03:54.111
- He's a great producer!

